{"event": "report", "t": 1795258383.524, "claim": "escalate", "verdict": {"verdict": "escalate", "root_cause": {"category": "missing_source", "model": "stg_payments", "summary": "stg_payments converts raw.payments.amount from cents to dollars, but raw.payments has no amount column (only id, order_id, payment_method). DuckDB reports this as a misleading 'cannot be referenced before it is defined' binder error. The fix belongs upstream in the ingestion job, not in the project."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "information_schema.columns where table_name='payments'", "finding": "raw.payments has only id, order_id, payment_method (3 rows). No amount column exists in any schema."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "information_schema.columns, all schemas", "finding": "No other table holds payment amounts; main has only stg_customers, stg_orders; raw has customers, orders, payments."}, {"kind": "log", "ref": "read_failure", "finding": "Build error is at model stg_payments: Binder Error on column amount; all downstream models skipped."}, {"kind": "commit", "ref": "inspect_history models/staging/stg_payments.sql and macros/cents_to_dollars.sql", "finding": "Only the initial commit a168b2c touched these; the model and macro logic have not changed recently, so the project code did not introduce the break."}], "changes": [], "confidence": "high"}, "diffs": [], "text": "I'm escalating this rather than fixing it, because the cause is outside the project. I made no file changes.\n\n**What failed:** `stg_payments` fails with a Binder Error on `amount`. The downstream models were skipped.\n\n**Root cause:** `stg_payments` converts `raw.payments.amount` from cents to dollars. But `raw.payments` has no `amount` column. It only has `id`, `order_id` and `payment_method`, and no other table in the database holds payment amounts. DuckDB's \"cannot be referenced before it is defined\" message is misleading here; the column is simply absent from the source.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- A query of `information_schema.columns` shows `raw.payments` has only three columns.\n- The same query across all schemas shows no other table with payment amounts.\n- The model and the `cents_to_dollars` macro are unchanged since the initial commit, so the project code did not introduce the break.\n\n**Why not fixed:** Inventing an amount column in the model or macro would fabricate revenue numbers. The ingestion job that loads `raw.payments` needs to restore the `amount` column, or the source needs to be pointed at the table that has it. Once that is done, rebuild `stg_payments+`.\n\n**Confidence:** high."}
